findings.recommendation:
Replace the fnmatch check with a strict allowlist of permitted page names, e.g.:
```php
$allowed = ['include.php', 'file1.php', 'file2.php', 'file3.php'];
if (!in_array($file, $allowed, true)) {
    echo "ERROR: File not found!";
    exit;
}
```
Alternatively, use `basename($file)` to strip path components and then validate, or enforce that `$file` contains no directory separators (`strpos($file, '/') === false && strpos($file, '\\') === false`).
